  "findings": {
    "physicalShape": "No canonical solid or contact shape changes: independent archive comparison preserves 75 native payloads and 47 existing object definitions; actual USDZ oriented triangle multisets and exact contact triangles preserved in all three exports. Whole views preserve open C curl and blocker coverage.",
    "partition": "Residual plateau_body is oak exterior and plateau_edge_18 is the sole contact. Metal/blocker are descriptor attachment roles with no contact IDs; all USDZ meshes unbound and no Material/Shader prims. Runtime picking remains an unperformed app check.",
    "cord": "Original meaningful shoulder bends had 4.5 mm surface gaps. Final whole paths bear at metal end lips and inner floor within declared .2 mm clearance. Final native proof has no unsupported meaningful bends; support and complete route share runtime Z=.012 m. No invented closed channel.",
    "loading": "Wood grip above metal curl, support below, source-consistent loading direction. Point support is a display estimate, not a modeled supplied carabiner or knot."
  },
